            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0443" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3296: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-08-28T09:00:00+01:00">August 28, 1933—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 30—6:24 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. Following exchanges have taken place in the Bolivia-Paraguay dispute: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>From Minister of Foreign Affairs Bio de Janeiro August 25 to President
                            of Council accepting in the name of ABCP League’s invitation
                            (Consulate’s 178, August 4, 10 a.m.) stating that the four powers are
                            proceeding in complete solidarity in negotiations with “belligerents” in
                            endeavoring to secure from them a “preliminary conciliation formula” and
                            that a definitive reply will shortly be made.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>From President of Council to Minister of Foreign Affairs, Rio de
                            Janeiro, August 26, conveying hope that an early success may result from
                            these efforts.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d311-f1"/></item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
